 only at tertullian.org in 2010, dedicated to the public domain in terms that permit free copying. Two things about it decide against landing it without saying so: it is one homily of six, and it is a translation of J. Bareille\'s 1865 FRENCH rather than of the Greek. A translation of a translation is a third claim again, and this project would have to render it as one — which is possible and has not been done, rather than impossible."], "absenceAuthors": ["Ambrose of Milan", "Jerome", "Augustine of Hippo", "Severian of Gabala", "Bede", "Alcuin of York", "Angelomus of Luxeuil", "Remigius of Auxerre"], "absenceWorks": ["Hexameron", "Liber quaestionum hebraicarum in Genesim", "De Genesi ad litteram", "In cosmogoniam homiliae sex", "In principium Genesis", "Interrogationes et responsiones in Genesim", "Commentarius in Genesim", "Commentarius in Genesim"], "sectionHeadings": ["14 fragments held here", "Believed to comment here — the acquisition list"], "asideNotes": ["Showing English translation only. This chapter is also held in the author’s own language and Latin translation.", "33 unreconciled lead entries on the acquisition record for this chapter, which omits its confidence. An entry establishes no distinct work, no possession and nothing renderable, and the list is not checked against the commentary above."], "leads": ["Alcuin of York — Interrogationes et responsiones in Genesim (804)", "Ambrose of Milan — Hexameron (397)", "Anastasius of Sinai — Hexaemeron (700)", "Augustine of Hippo — De Genesi ad litteram (430)", "Augustine of Hippo — De Genesi ad litteram imperfectus liber (430)", "Augustine of Hippo — De Genesi contra Manichaeos (430)", "Augustine of Hippo — Quaestiones in Heptateuchum (430)", "Basil of Caesarea — Homiliae in Hexaemeron (379)", "Basil the Great — Homiliae in Hexaemeron (379)", "Bede the Venerable — In principium Genesis (735)", "Bonaventure — Collationes in Hexaemeron (1274)", "Cornelius a Lapide — Commentaria in Scripturam Sacram (1637)", "C